commit 8e5274ea09d1ca0f4eb66938e7411264031f2787
Author: wormzjl <wormzjl@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Sep 25 03:42:01 2026 +0800

    Decide the network's phases with the equilibrium engine (P3 WP7)
    
    flashTP is now an adapter over FluidTpEquilibrium TP with the network's own
    free-water model (NetworkPhaseEngine): placement and boundary charges, the
    solver's seeds, the outer active-set check and the inventory refresh take
    the engine's stability test, split, critical band and free-water rule,
    stated with the network's own phase evaluations. The Wilson-started flash
    and the vaporBranch root heuristic are retired; PhaseIdentification is the
    one liquid/vapour rule. A critical-band failure is the typed
    CriticalBandHold on the existing hold path. A vessel of one pure
    hydrocarbon across its saturation line takes the engine's UV coexistence
    instead of flipping its slot, so a nitrogen tank condenses and boils.
    
    The two WP4 runtime failures: the trace-water flash cost (six-tank first
    slice 2,084,304 to 214,660 checkpoints) and fix E2, a pump connection's
    column is its suction's density (pumped line on its own steady state).
    
    Nitrogen, methane and the network envelope reach 10 MPa (fluid_domain;
    the crude_19 envelopes follow the loader rule, the cuts keep 2 MPa); the
    eight bundled pins are unchanged. A liquid-slot supercritical component
    takes its dilute viscosity. FORMULATION direct-liquid-v1:tp-engine-v1;
    the legacy digest is re-printed. Fresh world.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

